<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Welsh Marches</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as March of Wales, Marchia Wallie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Welsh <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marche">Marches</a> are the borderlands between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>. After 1066 Norman lords seized much of eastern and southern Wales and ruled it as marcher lordships with their own courts and laws, outside the normal English shires. The March remained a distinct zone until the Laws in Wales Acts of 1536 and 1543 turned it into new shires.</p></div>
